Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Qualcomm Sensor Core userspace library
 libssc talks to the sensors that Qualcomm's Sensor Core (SSC) serves over
 QRTR/QMI. It is what lets iio-sensor-proxy expose the accelerometer, ambient
 light, proximity and compass of a mainline Linux Qualcomm phone such as the
 Xiaomi POCO F5 / Redmi Note 12 Turbo (marble) on D-Bus.
 .
 The package ships libssc.so.2, ssccli (ssccli --sensor accelerometer is the
 quickest way to see whether the DSP side answers at all) and the headers plus
 pkg-config file that iio-sensor-proxy needs to build with -Dssc-support.
 .
 On marble the SSC service only appears on the QRTR bus a few seconds into the
 boot, so debian/patches makes the lookup wait for it instead of giving up on
 the first attempt.
